 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Covariance Validity:** The refined covariance matrix $\hat{\Sigma}$ is reconstructed from $\hat{l}$ as $\hat{\Sigma} = \hat{L}\hat{L}^\top$ (where $\hat{L}$ is the lower-triangular matrix from $\hat{l}$). This construction guarantees positive semi-definiteness by definition, avoiding invalid covariance matrices that might arise from direct perturbation of eigenvalues [S1].
-*   **Temporal Discontinuity:** The use of sinusoidal positional encodings helps capture periodic or high-frequency temporal changes, but if the time $t$ is not normalized or bounded appropriately, the high-frequency terms may oscillate wildly [S1].
+*   **Covariance Reconstruction:** The refined covariance matrix $\hat{\Sigma}$ is reconstructed from $\hat{l}$ as $\hat{\Sigma} = \hat{L}\hat{L}^\top$ (where $\hat{L}$ is the lower-triangular matrix from $\hat{l}$) [S1].
+*   **Training Dependency:** The method requires training the MLPs alongside the Gaussians, and the residuals are added directly to the vectorized covariance elements, which requires careful handling of numerical stability during optimization [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Computational Cost:** Adds the cost of two MLP forward passes per Gaussian per frame (or per refinement step). The MLPs are small ($C_{in} \times 64 \times C_{out}$), so the overhead is relatively low compared to the rasterization cost [S1].
-*   **Memory:** Requires storing the MLP weights. The number of parameters is small: $27 \times 64 + 64 \times C_{out}$ per MLP. With 4 MLPs, this is negligible compared to the Gaussian attributes [S1].
+*   **Computational Cost:** Adds the cost of four MLP forward passes per Gaussian per frame [S1]. The MLPs are small ($C_{in} \times 64 \times C_{out}$) [S1].
+*   **Memory:** Requires storing the MLP weights [S1]. The number of parameters is small: $27 \times 64 + 64 \times C_{out}$ per MLP [S1].
 *   **Strengths:** Enables accurate modeling of complex non-rigid deformations and time-varying appearance without increasing the number of Gaussians [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires training the MLPs alongside the Gaussians. The method is specific to 7D Gaussian Splatting (spatial-temporal-angular) and may not directly apply to static 3DGS without modification [S1].
